dthelp: pass1/eltdef must not build in parallel

Every other directory under cde/programs/dthelp/parser/ that generates
sources during the build carries a .NOTPARALLEL: -- sixteen of them, all
upstream.  pass1/eltdef is the one upstream missed, and it has the same
shape as its siblings:

    BUILT_SOURCES = $(CPRODS) $(EPRODS)
    $(CPRODS): CDONE       # context.h, delim.h -- generated from context.dat
    $(EPRODS): EDONE       # globdef.h, signon.h -- generated BY ./eltdef
    EDONE: eltdef ...

Satisfying EDONE means building eltdef, and eltutil.c #includes the
context.h that CDONE is still generating.  A fresh tree has empty .deps
files, so make does not know the object depends on that header and runs
both branches at once:

    eltutil.c:497:20: error: 'NEEDN' undeclared
    eltutil.c:503:20: error: 'GLOBDEF' undeclared; did you mean 'RGLOBDEF'?

Timing-dependent, so it hides -- two CI runs built this tree before one
failed.  .NOTPARALLEL applies to this makefile alone; the rest of CDE
still builds with -j.

--- a/programs/dthelp/parser/pass1/eltdef/Makefile.am
+++ b/programs/dthelp/parser/pass1/eltdef/Makefile.am
@@ -7,6 +7,24 @@
 ELTDEF = ./eltdef
 CONTEXT = $(HELPUTILSRC)/context
 
+# Every other directory under parser/ that generates sources this way
+# carries this; pass1/eltdef is the one upstream missed.  Without it,
+# BUILT_SOURCES' two branches race:
+#
+#     $(CPRODS): CDONE      # context.h, delim.h -- generated from context.dat
+#     $(EPRODS): EDONE      # globdef.h, signon.h -- generated BY ./eltdef
+#     EDONE: eltdef ...
+#
+# so satisfying EDONE builds eltdef, whose eltutil.c #includes the
+# context.h that CDONE is still writing.  On a fresh tree the .deps files
+# are empty, so make has no idea the object needs that header:
+#
+#     eltutil.c:497: error: 'NEEDN' undeclared
+#     eltutil.c:503: error: 'GLOBDEF' undeclared; did you mean 'RGLOBDEF'?
+#
+# It is timing-dependent, so it hides: the same tree built twice on CI
+# before it failed.
+.NOTPARALLEL:
 
 noinst_PROGRAMS = eltdef
 
